              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "$\\dfrac{n}{n + 3} \\times \\dfrac{n - 1}{n + 2} = \\dfrac{5}{12}$ gives $12n^2 - 12n = 5n^2 + 25n + 30$, so $7n^2 - 37n - 30 = 0$. Factorising: $(7n + 5)(n - 6) = 0$, so $n = 6$ (the negative root is impossible). With 6 red and 3 blue balls, P(both blue) $= \\frac{3}{9} \\times \\frac{2}{8} = \\frac{6}{72} = \\frac{1}{12}$.",
    "workedSolution": "1. $12n(n - 1) = 5(n + 3)(n + 2)$.\n2. $12n^2 - 12n = 5n^2 + 25n + 30$, so $7n^2 - 37n - 30 = 0$.\n3. $(7n + 5)(n - 6) = 0$: $n = 6$ or $n = -\\frac{5}{7}$; a number of balls must be a positive whole number, so $n = 6$.\n4. P(both blue) $= \\frac{3}{9} \\times \\frac{2}{8} = \\frac{1}{12} \\approx 0.0833$.",
    "hints": [
